config VIDEO_JPEGENC
	bool "Software JPEG encoder based on the jpegenc module"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ZEPHYR_VIDEO_JPEGENC_ENABLED
	depends on VIDEO_ENCODER_JPEG
	depends on ZEPHYR_JPEGENC_MODULE
	select JPEGENC
	help
	  Enable a software baseline JPEG encoder based on the jpegenc module.
	  It encodes NV12, YUV420, YUYV, RGB565 (either byte order) or GREY
	  frames and runs on any platform, including native_sim and QEMU. It
	  needs no heap: the encoder state (about 3.3 KiB) is part of the
	  device data, and the image is written directly into the output
	  buffer. Encoding runs in the thread calling video_enqueue(). The
	  quality control maps onto the encoder's four quality levels.
